From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: subtitles and OSD

Subtitle rendering for the AVFoundation video output.

Every object mpv's osd_render() returns with content (the primary and the
secondary subtitle, then the OSD) is drawn into one premultiplied BGRA
canvas in mpv's order, later objects over earlier ones. The engine Vivid
ships today shows only the last object; this one shows both subtitles. A
single object still gives exactly the same pixels. Objects whose drawn
parts are all at their own size use direct integer blends; the others go
through CoreGraphics, which draws each part at its own size. The canvas is
rendered again only when the set of objects or one of their change ids
changes. The bounding box is the union of the drawn parts, with each edge
clamped to the canvas on its own.

Pool surfaces are cleared with dirty tracking (up to four IOSurfaces, each
cleared only where it was last drawn). On the separate subtitle layer each
change becomes one timed sample at the video frame's presentation time;
when a cue ends, a cleared canvas replaces it. Compositing also keeps a
CoreGraphics snapshot for the Core Image path. Render counters feed a
verbose performance summary.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with Vivid's earlier patches.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
